00:10:36.359 --> 00:10:38.716
over the last three to four
years, and I love Dick Cusam,

00:10:38.716 --> 00:10:40.817
one of my best buds in business
and I saw him recently,

00:10:40.817 --> 00:10:43.881
but results are results,
meaning it didn't go good enough

00:10:43.881 --> 00:10:45.639
for him not to be excited
about the guy who invented

00:10:45.639 --> 00:10:47.984
it to be back in place,
though you might not like

00:10:47.984 --> 00:10:50.387
his personality, things of
that nature, but I hate when

00:10:50.387 --> 00:10:53.139
the media's like,
everything is so negative.

00:10:53.139 --> 00:10:57.306
Like when I buy a company,
and become a CEO of it,

00:10:57.306 --> 00:10:59.059
because that will happen
in my career, and there's

00:10:59.059 --> 00:11:02.218
an exodus, becaue big shot Gary is coming,

00:11:02.218 --> 00:11:04.693
let me promise you, anybody
that I wanted to keep

00:11:04.693 --> 00:11:06.505
would have stayed, because
I would convince them

00:11:06.505 --> 00:11:08.386
that I'm coming to do nothing but good.

00:11:08.386 --> 00:11:09.953
And maybe three or four
just wouldn't see it,

00:11:09.953 --> 00:11:11.774
or they were best buds
with the former CEO,

00:11:11.774 --> 00:11:13.191
or they're just tired.

00:11:13.191 --> 00:11:15.688
But please don't get
caught up in the hyperbole

00:11:15.688 --> 00:11:18.984
of there's a new CEO, we're
still witihin the year

00:11:18.984 --> 00:11:23.384
of that new CEO, this is
common business stuff, period.

00:11:23.384 --> 00:11:25.833
Like, this is what always
happens, so you don't know

00:11:25.833 --> 00:11:27.922
if they were forced out or
they were left on their own,

00:11:27.922 --> 00:11:29.723
I don't know, even though
I'm close to a lot of

00:11:29.723 --> 00:11:31.766
the people involved.

00:11:31.766 --> 00:11:33.851
Because when I read those
headlines, I poo poo them

00:11:33.851 --> 00:11:35.476
because I am an actual operator.

00:11:35.476 --> 00:11:38.286
I'm not confused by them, I
know what real business is.

00:11:38.286 --> 00:11:40.722
Jack's come in, he's got a
different plan, some pieces

00:11:40.722 --> 00:11:43.366
fit for that, some don't,
some people he might have

00:11:43.366 --> 00:11:45.804
wanted to fit for that, decided
they don't fit for that,

00:11:45.804 --> 00:11:49.089
it's just real life, it's
not some huge conspiracy.

00:11:49.089 --> 00:11:51.887
I think that's what I think.

00:11:51.887 --> 00:11:54.127
Like that's what it is, I
just wanted to answer this

00:11:54.127 --> 00:11:56.147
question because I'm
stunned by how many people

00:11:56.147 --> 00:11:59.248
just accept very basic
narratives, when if you live it

00:11:59.248 --> 00:12:01.825
you know the real details
underneath, just like you know

00:12:01.825 --> 00:12:02.927
anything that's in your world.

00:12:02.927 --> 00:12:05.365
My world is business, you know the real,

00:12:05.365 --> 00:12:06.806
I read headlines, I'm
like "oh," you're like

00:12:06.806 --> 00:12:08.844
"no, that's what really happened."

00:12:08.844 --> 00:12:11.827
Just like we've gotten
cynical to "leave of absence."

00:12:11.827 --> 00:12:14.962
Did you see "Spotlight?"
- No.

00:12:14.963 --> 00:12:17.610
- Okay, it was about the priest
that did sexual harassment.

00:12:17.610 --> 00:12:18.992
- Oh yeah, I heard about it.

00:12:18.992 --> 00:12:21.266
- Their official, when
they were doing bad things

00:12:21.266 --> 00:12:25.527
was they got relocated on
assignment, or "sick leave."

00:12:25.527 --> 00:12:26.712
"Sick leave."

00:12:26.712 --> 00:12:30.428
So this "exodus" may
be on strategy, get it?

00:12:32.360 --> 00:12:35.496
Question of the day, actually educate me.

00:12:35.496 --> 00:12:37.515
Tell me something that
happened in your world

00:12:37.515 --> 00:12:39.872
and how it's explained,
but what's really going on.

00:12:39.872 --> 00:12:41.822
Could be some fun late night reading.

00:12:41.822 --> 00:12:42.555
- I'll be reading it.

00:12:42.555 --> 00:12:43.981
- Yeah, I'm going to Phoenix
tonight so hopefully,

00:12:43.981 --> 00:12:45.456
oh actually this is airing tomorrow.

00:12:45.456 --> 00:12:47.871
We're doing a little bit of
smarter cadence on the shows,

00:12:47.871 --> 00:12:49.793
it doesn't have to go out immediately.

00:12:49.793 --> 00:12:53.904
You keep asking questions,
I'll keep answering them.

00:12:53.904 --> 00:12:58.170
(upbeat music)

